.custom = .{ .doc_section = "Reference" },
---
These defaults come from the LLMD source reviewed on 16 November 2026.
Use `--name=value` for an option with a value and a bare flag for a boolean
switch.

# [Model flags]($heading.id('model-and-listener'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--model=<path>` | Required | Path to a model directory or supported model URI. |
| `--model-name=<text>` | Basename of the model path | Set the identifier reported by `/v1/models` and used in requests. |

# [Bind the listener]($heading.id('bind-the-listener'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--listen=<address>` | `0.0.0.0:8000` | Bind HTTP to an IP address and port. A bare IPv4 address uses port `8000`. |

# [Launch by model source]($heading.id('launch-by-model-source'))

```=html
<fieldset class="command-tabs model-walkthrough" data-toc-parent="launch-by-model-source">
  <legend>Model source</legend>
  <div class="model-stage">
    <label id="model-source-local" class="command-tab" data-toc-label="Local directory"><input type="radio" name="model-source" aria-controls="model-command-local" checked><span>Local directory</span></label>
    <div class="model-stage-panel" id="model-command-local">
      <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy local launch command">llmd --model="${HOME}/models/Qwen/Qwen3-4B" \
  --model-name=qwen3-4b \
  --listen=127.0.0.1:8000
</code></pre>
      <p>Point LLMD to a directory with the <a href="#local-model-files">configuration, tokenizer and weights</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="model-stage">
    <label id="model-source-hugging-face" class="command-tab" data-toc-label="Hugging Face"><input type="radio" name="model-source" aria-controls="model-command-hugging-face"><span>Hugging Face</span></label>
    <div class="model-stage-panel" id="model-command-hugging-face">
      <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy Hugging Face launch command">llmd --model=hf://Qwen/Qwen3-4B \
  --model-name=qwen3-4b \
  --listen=127.0.0.1:8000
</code></pre>
      <p>Append <code>@revision</code> to pin a revision. Set <code>HF_TOKEN</code> for gated access.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="model-stage">
    <label id="model-source-s3" class="command-tab" data-toc-label="S3"><input type="radio" name="model-source" aria-controls="model-command-s3"><span>S3</span></label>
    <div class="model-stage-panel" id="model-command-s3">
      <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy S3 launch command">llmd --model=s3://my-bucket/llm/Qwen3-4B \
  --model-name=qwen3-4b \
  --listen=127.0.0.1:8000
</code></pre>
      <p>Replace the bucket and prefix. For private storage, configure <a href="#cloud-model-uris">AWS credentials</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="model-stage">
    <label id="model-source-gcs" class="command-tab" data-toc-label="GCS"><input type="radio" name="model-source" aria-controls="model-command-gcs"><span>GCS</span></label>
    <div class="model-stage-panel" id="model-command-gcs">
      <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy GCS launch command">llmd --model=gs://my-bucket/llm/Qwen3-4B \
  --model-name=qwen3-4b \
  --listen=127.0.0.1:8000
</code></pre>
      <p>Replace the bucket and prefix. For private storage, configure <a href="#cloud-model-uris">Google Cloud credentials</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</fieldset>
```

- `--model` selects the directory or URI.
- `--model-name` makes the examples serve `qwen3-4b`. Verify the ID with [Models]($link.page('llmd/reference/v1/models')).
- `--listen` binds these native examples to `127.0.0.1:8000` for local access.

# [Model storage prerequisites]($heading.id('model-storage-prerequisites'))

## [Local model files]($heading.id('local-model-files'))

Point `--model` to the directory containing `config.json`. Keep the tokenizer,
Safetensors weights, weight index and all its shards, and any supplied chat
template or generation settings together from the same revision.
`Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B` also needs its sentence-transformers module and
pooling configuration files.

In [Any model, any platform]($link.page('llmd/tutorial/start')), **Download first**
generates a host command that saves the model under `${HOME}/models/<org>/<model>`.
To pin a download, add `--revision <commit>` to that command and give each
revision its own local directory. Native LLMD reads the host path directly.
For Docker, see [Run a local model]($link.page('llmd/reference/docker-options').ref('run-a-local-checkpoint')).

## [Cloud model URIs]($heading.id('cloud-model-uris'))

Use `--model=hf://org/repo@revision` to select a Hugging Face revision at
launch. For S3 or Google Cloud Storage, keep the model files together under
one bucket prefix and pass `--model=s3://my-bucket/llm/model` or
`--model=gs://my-bucket/llm/model`. To adapt a generated launch command, choose
**Load at launch** and replace its `--model` value with the bucket URI.
Configure [model storage credentials]($link.page('llmd/reference/environment-variables').unsafeRef('model-storage-and-credentials'))
in the environment that runs LLMD. See [Environment variables]($link.page('llmd/reference/environment-variables'))
for proxy settings and diagnostics.

# [Select the I/O implementation]($heading.id('io-implementation'))

The reviewed source exposes this advanced option. Check availability in
your LLMD build.

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--io-impl=<name>` | `zio` | Choose the I/O implementation. `threaded` is also available in the reviewed source. |

# [Check installed flags]($heading.id('check-installed-flags'))

Check the help from your installed binary or container for the options
it exposes. The CUDA recipe in
[Any model, any platform]($link.page('llmd/tutorial/start').unsafeRef('lfm3-fp8-cuda')) uses
`zmlai/llmd:cuda`. Docker options go before the image name. LLMD options go
after it.

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `-h`, `--help` | Off | Print the supported usage. |

```sh
# Native installation
llmd --help

# CUDA container
docker run --rm zmlai/llmd:cuda --help
```
